1
00:00:28,280 --> 00:00:30,960
Easily leaping beyond the same era

2
00:00:32,780 --> 00:00:37,440
diving into the city,
playing at being a hero

3
00:00:37,440 --> 00:00:39,500
I wanna turn into a paradise

4
00:00:39,500 --> 00:00:42,180
Nothing but the latest trends

5
00:00:42,180 --> 00:00:45,080
as we keep wearing them

6
00:00:45,080 --> 00:00:49,240
because a bare face suits us even more

7
00:00:49,240 --> 00:00:51,060
Let it ring!

8
00:00:51,600 --> 00:00:55,020
Everybody can do, we started running

9
00:00:55,020 --> 00:00:58,240
Dreams never stop, you know

10
00:00:58,240 --> 00:01:02,480
Let's go out and face tomorrow too

11
00:01:02,480 --> 00:01:03,740
Ladies' world

12
00:01:03,740 --> 00:01:06,140
Everybody can do

13
00:01:06,140 --> 00:01:10,860
It doesn't hurt if we stray a little

14
00:01:10,860 --> 00:01:15,000
holding onto our noisy curiosity

15
00:01:15,680 --> 00:01:17,860
we kept it strong and high

16
00:01:29,200 --> 00:01:30,940
Ryo-san's Great Escape

17
00:01:42,500 --> 00:01:43,520
Ohara-kun

18
00:01:43,520 --> 00:01:43,860
Yes?

19
00:01:44,380 --> 00:01:48,500
After watching that video, what on earth kind
of training are you giving your subordinates?

20
00:01:48,500 --> 00:01:51,400
In the station's internal survey,
the Kameari Kōen-mae police box

21
00:01:51,400 --> 00:01:56,420
was proudly ranked first among the police
boxes everyone least wants to be assigned to.

22
00:01:56,420 --> 00:01:57,380
Ryotsu, sir.

23
00:01:57,380 --> 00:01:59,840
It's entirely the fault of that one idiot.

24
00:01:59,840 --> 00:02:02,280
Thanks to him, our police box

25
00:02:07,360 --> 00:02:08,780
I understand how you feel.

26
00:02:09,240 --> 00:02:12,440
But unless we rein in Ryotsu,
it will affect your promotion too.

27
00:02:12,440 --> 00:02:16,540
No, no, at this rate,
my own neck could be on the line too.

28
00:02:16,540 --> 00:02:18,000
Please, I'm counting on you.

29
00:02:18,500 --> 00:02:19,160
Ohara-kun.

30
00:02:27,020 --> 00:02:29,580
Now, which one should I play with today?

31
00:02:30,480 --> 00:02:31,360
Ryo-san

32
00:02:31,360 --> 00:02:32,780
Today's the Tora-Kame...

33
00:02:34,760 --> 00:02:36,140
There's nobody here.

34
00:02:36,140 --> 00:02:36,940
Which damn one?

35
00:02:38,120 --> 00:02:39,040
Bases loaded, we're in trouble.

36
00:02:39,040 --> 00:02:40,320
Put some guts into it and throw!

37
00:02:42,220 --> 00:02:44,700
We got them down to two
strikes after all that effort.

38
00:02:45,700 --> 00:02:46,700
Just as I thought.

39
00:02:49,500 --> 00:02:54,400
Hey, if Junpei and Kappe are watching,
I win if I shut them out this inning.

40
00:02:55,840 --> 00:02:57,080
Excuse me.

41
00:02:59,200 --> 00:03:00,280
He's always apologizing.

42
00:03:00,660 --> 00:03:01,960
This way, please.

43
00:03:02,620 --> 00:03:03,200
Y-yes.

44
00:03:04,260 --> 00:03:05,500
Officer...

45
00:03:05,900 --> 00:03:08,180
I had an accident and crashed
my car into the guardrail.

46
00:03:12,480 --> 00:03:13,520
You guys!

47
00:03:13,860 --> 00:03:16,980
You called out at the worst time,
and now I'm all rattled!

48
00:03:17,260 --> 00:03:19,740
N-no, I just... the car...

49
00:03:19,740 --> 00:03:21,580
I'm on my break right now.

50
00:03:21,580 --> 00:03:23,500
If you're coming, come later!

51
00:03:23,820 --> 00:03:25,420
Y-yes...

52
00:03:27,640 --> 00:03:28,620
That's a lead.

53
00:03:28,620 --> 00:03:31,140
No matter what,
I won't let any more runs score!

54
00:03:31,140 --> 00:03:32,220
Sorry.

55
00:03:32,220 --> 00:03:33,200
It's happening again.

56
00:03:33,200 --> 00:03:33,960
Yes.

57
00:03:37,020 --> 00:03:39,480
Which way was Kameari Public Hall again?

58
00:03:40,480 --> 00:03:41,440
Whoa!

59
00:03:41,440 --> 00:03:42,180
Aaaaah!

60
00:03:44,140 --> 00:03:45,940
G-goodbye, Mike.

61
00:03:45,940 --> 00:03:47,260
How lame.

62
00:03:47,260 --> 00:03:48,480
Let's go home, let's go home.

63
00:03:48,480 --> 00:03:51,320
That Kameari Public...

64
00:03:51,320 --> 00:03:52,320
Yah!

65
00:04:10,800 --> 00:04:13,900
We lost because of you, you know.

66
00:04:13,900 --> 00:04:15,880
Let's start with the first race.

67
00:04:16,420 --> 00:04:18,600
Your personality really comes through,
doesn't it.

68
00:04:18,600 --> 00:04:19,640
Well, of course.

69
00:04:19,640 --> 00:04:21,860
For me, this is basically my real job.

70
00:04:24,340 --> 00:04:25,420
That voice...

71
00:04:30,160 --> 00:04:31,000
Chief!

72
00:04:32,100 --> 00:04:33,560
Lovely weather today.

73
00:04:34,380 --> 00:04:36,400
Ryo-san, come here a sec.

74
00:04:36,400 --> 00:04:38,380
Ow ow!

75
00:04:39,060 --> 00:04:42,000
It's strange, the Chief isn't angry at all.

76
00:04:43,900 --> 00:04:44,760
He's gone past angry.

77
00:04:45,240 --> 00:04:46,040
Look at this.

78
00:04:50,440 --> 00:04:53,560
It was caught on the security camera at the
convenience store in front of the station.

79
00:04:56,100 --> 00:04:56,880
It's our senior officer.

80
00:04:58,560 --> 00:04:59,580
What is he doing?

81
00:05:00,640 --> 00:05:03,940
Ugh, he's peeling off only
the prize entry stickers.

82
00:05:04,440 --> 00:05:05,400
That's not all.

83
00:05:06,080 --> 00:05:07,560
Now he's moved on to the ice cream.

84
00:05:08,180 --> 00:05:09,100
What's he doing?

85
00:05:10,100 --> 00:05:13,060
He's pulling out the ice cream sticks
to check whether they're winners.

86
00:05:14,520 --> 00:05:18,040
Now he's buying bread...
I wonder what he's checking.

87
00:05:19,900 --> 00:05:24,960
I get it, he's checking the dates. Even
though he eats spoiled food without a care

88
00:05:28,300 --> 00:05:30,960
He's trying to grab the one
with the newer date in the back.

89
00:05:32,720 --> 00:05:37,200
Aaah, you two caused a panic.

90
00:05:38,760 --> 00:05:39,680
Well, about that...

91
00:05:39,680 --> 00:05:40,880
Don't "well" me.

92
00:05:40,880 --> 00:05:43,420
Your actions driven by your greed

93
00:05:43,420 --> 00:05:46,460
The store staff are seriously troubled,
and we've received complaints.

94
00:05:46,460 --> 00:05:47,660
No wonder.

95
00:05:47,660 --> 00:05:48,780
And that's not all.

96
00:05:49,140 --> 00:05:51,420
Pachinko parlor security
cameras also caught you,

97
00:05:51,420 --> 00:05:52,660
as did the arcade's,

98
00:05:52,660 --> 00:05:54,620
and the adult video specialty shop's.

99
00:05:54,620 --> 00:05:56,040
You're on all of them.

100
00:05:56,460 --> 00:05:57,260
But, Chief.

101
00:05:57,260 --> 00:05:59,840
Those were all outside of working hours.

102
00:05:59,840 --> 00:06:00,680
Liar.

103
00:06:01,340 --> 00:06:04,020
From today,
I'll be glued to you 24 hours a day

104
00:06:04,020 --> 00:06:05,640
and keep an eye on everything you do.

105
00:06:05,640 --> 00:06:06,820
Don't make excuses.

106
00:06:07,200 --> 00:06:28,600
Uuuugh...

107
00:06:28,600 --> 00:06:29,760
I wonder if you've got the wrong idea.

108
00:06:30,240 --> 00:06:31,400
Ryo-san!

109
00:06:31,400 --> 00:06:35,060
That barbecue party in the park the other day was fun,
wasn't it?

110
00:06:35,060 --> 00:06:36,080
Let's do it again.

111
00:06:36,080 --> 00:06:37,840
You've got the wrong person. It wasn't me.

112
00:06:38,560 --> 00:06:39,920
What are you talking about?

113
00:06:39,920 --> 00:06:42,320
Look, I gathered up my buddies and all.

114
00:06:42,320 --> 00:06:42,940
Whoa!

115
00:06:44,420 --> 00:06:47,860
Was it you who started a small
fire with a bonfire in the park?

116
00:06:47,860 --> 00:06:49,220
No, it wasn't me, not me!

117
00:06:49,220 --> 00:06:50,880
I swear it wasn't me.

118
00:07:04,160 --> 00:07:04,800
That's right.

119
00:07:04,800 --> 00:07:07,420
Today was the first shrine
visit for Dora Kame Seven.

120
00:07:09,060 --> 00:07:10,380
How could I forget?

121
00:07:12,460 --> 00:07:13,720
What's with that face?

122
00:07:13,720 --> 00:07:15,580
No, it's nothing.

123
00:07:16,280 --> 00:07:18,380
Stop it, you creep.

124
00:07:18,380 --> 00:07:20,160
That'll be 680 yen.

125
00:07:24,960 --> 00:07:26,100
This is bad.

126
00:07:26,100 --> 00:07:28,060
Ryotsu, find him right away!

127
00:07:29,040 --> 00:07:29,820
Search for him!

128
00:07:29,820 --> 00:07:30,360
Yes, sir.

129
00:07:36,900 --> 00:07:38,200
Sorry about that.

130
00:07:39,120 --> 00:07:40,420
While we're wasting time like this,

131
00:07:40,420 --> 00:07:42,340
Dora Kame Seven will sell out!

132
00:07:48,320 --> 00:07:49,640
Dora Kame Seven -

133
00:07:49,640 --> 00:07:50,840
Dora Kame Seven -

134
00:07:56,960 --> 00:07:58,940
What's the big rush?

135
00:07:59,840 --> 00:08:00,640
No, that's not -

136
00:08:02,600 --> 00:08:05,120
Dora Kame Seven's gonna sell out,
Dora Kame Seven -

137
00:08:05,120 --> 00:08:07,300
Yeah, this isn't good for your body.

138
00:08:07,300 --> 00:08:09,320
Come what may!

139
00:08:11,300 --> 00:08:12,600
Hey, wait, Ryotsu!

140
00:08:13,160 --> 00:08:14,120
What's all the commotion?

141
00:08:18,940 --> 00:08:21,020
Dora Kame Seven,
Dora Kame Seven, Dora Kame Seven!

142
00:08:21,620 --> 00:08:22,420
Ryotsu!

143
00:08:24,040 --> 00:08:25,080
Wait, hey!

144
00:08:32,960 --> 00:08:34,560
Damn it, where did he go?

145
00:08:48,080 --> 00:08:50,760
Ryotsu! You think you can escape these legs?

146
00:08:50,920 --> 00:08:54,600
Ugh! Take him down, Chief!
Dora Kame Seven's gonna sell out!

147
00:08:56,140 --> 00:08:57,540
So you dragged him back here?

148
00:08:57,540 --> 00:09:01,460
Trying to run off just
to buy a brand-new game!

149
00:09:01,460 --> 00:09:02,760
That's just like Ryo-chan, isn't it.

150
00:09:03,300 --> 00:09:05,400
At this point,
we should just put a rope around his neck

151
00:09:05,760 --> 00:09:09,340
and walk him around like a dog.
There's no other way to manage this man.

152
00:09:09,340 --> 00:09:11,160
With all due respect, Chief,

153
00:09:11,160 --> 00:09:15,100
trying to monitor one man's
every move day and night

154
00:09:15,100 --> 00:09:16,740
was impossible from the start.

155
00:09:16,740 --> 00:09:17,280
What did you say?

156
00:09:17,280 --> 00:09:20,580
Who do you think is
causing me all this trouble?

157
00:09:20,580 --> 00:09:22,440
If you're that worried about what I do,

158
00:09:22,440 --> 00:09:25,300
then just build a jail cell and lock me up.

159
00:09:25,300 --> 00:09:26,260
You said it.

160
00:09:27,540 --> 00:09:29,980
Fine, let's do it!
A proper tatami jail-loan!

161
00:09:36,380 --> 00:09:46,300
This is your office, your betting den, your home sweet home. I've got the chief's permission.
You, the walking tabloid headline, start working inside this cell from today.

162
00:09:46,300 --> 00:09:54,500
Let me out! I hate this place! No games, no model kits, no TV!
/ Shaking it won't break it, you know.

163
00:09:54,900 --> 00:09:58,520
Damn it, you'll remember this!
I'm getting out of here, mark my words.

164
00:10:23,680 --> 00:10:24,820
Just watch me.

165
00:10:28,520 --> 00:10:29,320
Ngh ahh

166
00:10:36,040 --> 00:10:37,240
No problem.

167
00:10:41,980 --> 00:10:44,460
What's wrong? It suddenly got heavy!

168
00:10:50,520 --> 00:10:52,740
It's a big one, Ryo-kun.

169
00:10:55,600 --> 00:10:58,160
Stop struggling in vain, Ryotsu!

170
00:11:00,800 --> 00:11:02,660
Where did you get something like this?

171
00:11:02,660 --> 00:11:04,460
I'm holding onto this, got it?

172
00:11:06,360 --> 00:11:08,280
The real show is only just beginning.

173
00:11:08,720 --> 00:11:10,300
I'm definitely going to escape from here.

174
00:11:35,040 --> 00:11:36,660
This is no joke!

175
00:11:36,660 --> 00:11:38,880
No TV, no radio, no manga either.

176
00:11:39,420 --> 00:11:40,880
During the day, it's all sorting out work.

177
00:11:40,880 --> 00:11:42,740
And at night, it's for spiritual training.

178
00:11:42,740 --> 00:11:43,480
Sutra copying,

179
00:11:44,280 --> 00:11:45,540
I can't take it.

180
00:11:46,920 --> 00:11:48,260
Even the pillars are the hardest.

181
00:11:48,260 --> 00:11:49,980
They're made of oak, you know.

182
00:11:49,980 --> 00:11:52,580
It would take a year to gnaw
through them with my teeth.

183
00:11:53,420 --> 00:11:56,120
I need to get some tools
if I'm going to escape.

184
00:12:02,100 --> 00:12:02,720
That one...

185
00:12:03,300 --> 00:12:04,780
Those tofu shop Gazu guys.

186
00:12:05,420 --> 00:12:05,820
Yeah.

187
00:12:12,220 --> 00:12:14,240
I'll need that and that.

188
00:12:23,560 --> 00:12:25,180
Wish me luck.

189
00:12:27,720 --> 00:12:30,760
Damn it.

190
00:12:36,620 --> 00:12:39,420
Got it!

191
00:12:39,420 --> 00:12:45,580
That idiot's here!

192
00:12:49,980 --> 00:12:50,620
This time for sure!

193
00:12:51,180 --> 00:12:52,900
Alright!

194
00:12:57,240 --> 00:12:58,440
What's this?

195
00:13:00,400 --> 00:13:03,280
Right now, I...

196
00:13:16,500 --> 00:13:17,700
Here you go!

197
00:13:17,760 --> 00:13:18,880
Thanks!

198
00:13:20,260 --> 00:13:21,340
I know, I know.

199
00:13:21,340 --> 00:13:23,280
What about the game cartridge we promised?

200
00:13:23,660 --> 00:13:24,460
I know.

201
00:13:25,540 --> 00:13:26,360
Yay!

202
00:13:26,780 --> 00:13:28,540
By the way, did you guys play Dora Kame?

203
00:13:28,580 --> 00:13:29,540
Of course we did.

204
00:13:29,540 --> 00:13:30,680
Lucky you.

205
00:13:30,680 --> 00:13:32,640
If you manage to escape,
come over to my place.

206
00:13:32,640 --> 00:13:33,980
I'll let you play it, so.

207
00:13:33,980 --> 00:13:34,680
Really?

208
00:13:35,060 --> 00:13:35,380
Yeah.

209
00:13:35,880 --> 00:13:36,860
Alright, just you wait.

210
00:13:36,860 --> 00:13:39,340
We'll definitely come, you'll see!

211
00:13:43,640 --> 00:13:46,220
Do you think Ryotsu has
learned his lesson at all?

212
00:13:46,860 --> 00:13:47,860
Well, who knows.

213
00:13:47,860 --> 00:13:49,820
He seems to be behaving himself, though.

214
00:14:04,380 --> 00:14:08,220
Cut the power to the police box,
then slip out in the confusion.

215
00:14:14,180 --> 00:14:15,180
What, a blackout?

216
00:14:17,020 --> 00:14:19,240
I'm sure there are candles here somewhere.

217
00:14:19,240 --> 00:14:20,680
Now's my chance.

218
00:14:24,140 --> 00:14:25,680
Ugh, damn it.

219
00:14:27,580 --> 00:14:29,660
Chief, what's wrong?

220
00:14:32,240 --> 00:14:33,600
No way...

221
00:14:34,440 --> 00:14:35,260
Ryotsu!

222
00:14:35,260 --> 00:14:38,420
Is he there?

223
00:14:38,420 --> 00:14:40,940
Sorry, Chief, I'm reflecting on my actions.

224
00:14:40,940 --> 00:14:42,580
That's right, that's right.

225
00:14:43,080 --> 00:14:48,520
How about it, Ryotsu? Sitting there, I bet
your past foolishness is really sinking in.

226
00:14:48,520 --> 00:14:51,220
Sorry, Chief, I'm reflecting on my actions.

227
00:14:51,220 --> 00:14:53,520
Good. Keep up the good work.

228
00:14:54,020 --> 00:14:57,200
Even Ryotsu seems to have
been affected this time.

229
00:14:57,640 --> 00:15:00,300
He just keeps saying
"I'm reflecting" like a parrot.

230
00:15:00,300 --> 00:15:02,920
That guy isn't the type to really reflect.

231
00:15:03,540 --> 00:15:05,020
Hand over the keys.

232
00:15:05,020 --> 00:15:06,100
Y-yes, sir.

233
00:15:06,100 --> 00:15:06,300
Yes.

234
00:15:09,200 --> 00:15:10,480
Hey, Ryotsu!

235
00:15:10,820 --> 00:15:12,880
What are you scheming now?

236
00:15:12,880 --> 00:15:13,340
Hey!

237
00:15:13,340 --> 00:15:13,940
Whoa!

238
00:15:13,940 --> 00:15:15,000
I'm sorry, Chief.

239
00:15:15,000 --> 00:15:15,980
I'm reflecting on my behavior.

240
00:15:15,980 --> 00:15:17,040
I'm sorry, Chief.

241
00:15:17,040 --> 00:15:18,040
I'm reflecting on my behavior.

242
00:15:18,040 --> 00:15:19,380
I'm sorry, Chief.

243
00:15:19,380 --> 00:15:20,600
I'm reflecting on my behavior.

244
00:15:20,600 --> 00:15:21,880
Sorry.

245
00:15:21,880 --> 00:15:22,620
Sorry.

246
00:15:22,620 --> 00:15:23,660
Chief, Chief.

247
00:15:23,660 --> 00:15:24,740
I'm reflecting on my behavior.

248
00:15:24,740 --> 00:15:26,160
I'm sorry, Chief.

249
00:15:26,160 --> 00:15:26,200
This is

250
00:15:26,200 --> 00:15:27,060
I'm reflecting on my behavior.

251
00:15:27,060 --> 00:15:28,160
I'm sorry, Chief.

252
00:15:28,160 --> 00:15:29,440
I'm reflecting on my behavior.

253
00:15:29,440 --> 00:15:31,160
You've got guts, Ryo-chan.

254
00:15:31,160 --> 00:15:33,720
Damn you, you clever little brat.

255
00:15:36,420 --> 00:15:37,980
So that earlier one was

256
00:15:39,440 --> 00:15:40,440
Ryotsu!

257
00:15:40,440 --> 00:15:41,200
Shit.

258
00:15:42,580 --> 00:15:44,000
I won't let you escape, Ryotsu.

259
00:15:50,300 --> 00:15:55,940
How about that?

260
00:15:57,200 --> 00:15:59,000
It was so close

261
00:16:07,440 --> 00:16:08,520
How's that, Ryotsu?

262
00:16:09,380 --> 00:16:14,460
This barbed wire covers everything up to the ceiling,
like a bug cage.

263
00:16:15,160 --> 00:16:16,340
What's more,

264
00:16:20,920 --> 00:16:25,140
as you can see, high-voltage
current runs through the barbed wire.

265
00:16:26,820 --> 00:16:28,320
How's that, Ryotsu?

266
00:16:30,260 --> 00:16:31,660
They've gone this far?

267
00:16:31,660 --> 00:16:34,200
Damn, if it's come to this,
it's our last resort.

268
00:16:37,960 --> 00:16:39,360
How is Ryotsu doing?

269
00:16:40,220 --> 00:16:42,340
He seems to be quietly keeping to himself.

270
00:16:42,340 --> 00:16:45,500
Good. This time there's really
no gap for him to escape through.

271
00:16:45,500 --> 00:16:47,100
But don't let your guard down.

272
00:16:53,480 --> 00:16:55,920
Any moment now, Harry from the first tunnel

273
00:16:55,920 --> 00:16:57,900
should be coming out past the bridge.

274
00:17:19,680 --> 00:17:21,560
Didn't that sound strange just now?

275
00:17:21,560 --> 00:17:22,840
A strange sound?

276
00:17:22,840 --> 00:17:25,120
I must be imagining it.

277
00:17:25,120 --> 00:17:30,940
I'm sure it wasn't finished yet.

278
00:17:32,180 --> 00:17:34,960
What's this? The floor is lifting up!

279
00:17:36,880 --> 00:17:38,740
Hey, quiet down, you!

280
00:17:39,540 --> 00:17:42,400
Hup, hup, hup, hup!

281
00:17:42,400 --> 00:17:44,480
Jump-sa, get out of the way!

282
00:17:44,480 --> 00:17:45,840
Kiiii!

283
00:17:45,840 --> 00:17:47,520
Ugh, ugh, ugh.

284
00:17:47,520 --> 00:17:50,540
Whoa, stop it!
Gah, ngh, ngh, stop it! Kiiii!

285
00:17:50,540 --> 00:17:51,322
Haa...

286
00:17:51,372 --> 00:17:55,260
I really think I heard a strange sound.

287
00:17:55,620 --> 00:17:58,220
Ugh, ugh, ugh, ugh.

288
00:18:08,840 --> 00:18:10,380
Could it be that Ryotsu

289
00:18:10,380 --> 00:18:14,520
is up to something?

290
00:18:14,520 --> 00:18:25,460
What's with that getup?

291
00:18:25,460 --> 00:18:28,540
I got too caught up earlier, so I got hot.

292
00:18:29,460 --> 00:18:30,700
What's with the helmet?

293
00:18:30,960 --> 00:18:34,480
Well, I figured I should protect my eyes.

294
00:18:34,820 --> 00:18:35,960
And the rope?

295
00:18:36,040 --> 00:18:37,781
It's fashion, Chief.

296
00:18:37,831 --> 00:18:40,220
It's all the rage lately. Don't you know?

297
00:18:43,820 --> 00:18:45,679
The first tunnel's end is,

298
00:18:45,729 --> 00:18:48,020
beyond repair now, so.

299
00:18:49,160 --> 00:18:51,580
Let's start on the second tunnel.

300
00:18:52,360 --> 00:18:54,580
Alright,
we're digging through the night tonight!

301
00:19:07,240 --> 00:19:08,560
It's empty.

302
00:19:08,560 --> 00:19:10,080
I'll go put it in.

303
00:19:10,820 --> 00:19:12,320
It's fine, it's fine.

304
00:19:16,640 --> 00:19:18,460
I went and broke the seed gun.

305
00:19:18,460 --> 00:19:18,820
Dammit!

306
00:19:26,060 --> 00:19:28,780
Come on, I, I, I've got to, got to go -

307
00:19:28,780 --> 00:19:31,040
That's strange.

308
00:19:31,040 --> 00:19:33,340
Whoa, w-what is it?

309
00:19:34,860 --> 00:19:36,320
Ryotsu, dammit!

310
00:19:36,320 --> 00:19:37,400
S-shoot, this is bad.

311
00:19:37,400 --> 00:19:38,720
Ryotsu.

312
00:19:38,720 --> 00:19:45,280
Hanya, hanya, here we go again, hanya.

313
00:19:45,280 --> 00:19:46,900
If Shinto is destroyed,

314
00:19:50,940 --> 00:19:52,140
That should do it.

315
00:19:53,000 --> 00:19:56,000
But we can't just keep
going straight like this.

316
00:19:58,460 --> 00:19:59,840
Alright, this way.

317
00:20:10,100 --> 00:20:13,220
So this one's a sewer pipe.

318
00:20:13,220 --> 00:20:15,740
Then it's this way.

319
00:21:03,720 --> 00:21:07,980
Yes! I've escaped! I'm free!

320
00:21:10,960 --> 00:21:14,180
Just you wait,
I'll get my revenge on you all!

321
00:21:14,180 --> 00:21:16,240
Ryotsu has escaped?

322
00:21:20,580 --> 00:21:22,500
Is he a mole or something?

323
00:21:22,500 --> 00:21:25,380
Right, find Ryotsu at once! Hurry!

324
00:21:25,380 --> 00:21:25,820
Yes.

325
00:21:38,260 --> 00:21:38,740
Yes!

326
00:21:38,740 --> 00:21:39,740
We can't get out like this!

327
00:21:39,940 --> 00:21:41,460
This is Ryotsu's doing!

328
00:21:43,620 --> 00:21:45,220
Exactly!

329
00:21:45,240 --> 00:21:46,980
Ryotsu! You bastard!

330
00:21:47,720 --> 00:21:48,200
Alright!

331
00:21:50,920 --> 00:21:54,320
In my right hand, 100 cockroaches,

332
00:21:56,060 --> 00:21:59,180
in my left, 100 bees.

333
00:22:00,580 --> 00:22:02,700
So, which one do you want
me to put down your pants?

334
00:22:03,120 --> 00:22:05,400
Where did you even get those things?

335
00:22:05,760 --> 00:22:07,500
Stop this idiotic nonsense!

336
00:22:08,020 --> 00:22:10,460
Oh, so you want both?

337
00:22:10,720 --> 00:22:12,060
Well then, here you go, end-rack!

338
00:22:20,400 --> 00:22:23,700
And as a bonus, smoke screens
and firecrackers too, that's me!

339
00:22:27,420 --> 00:22:29,200
Aaaaaah!

340
00:22:33,300 --> 00:22:36,820
How about that?
This is what happens when you cross me!

341
00:22:38,100 --> 00:22:39,860
Ugh, they're gathering!

342
00:22:39,860 --> 00:22:41,460
Got you! Here they come!

343
00:22:41,460 --> 00:22:43,940
Ow The barbed wire's on my back!

344
00:22:50,020 --> 00:22:52,280
I wonder if Ohara-kun is doing all right.

345
00:22:56,200 --> 00:22:57,340
Don't push!

346
00:23:00,360 --> 00:23:01,760
Please, help me!

347
00:23:01,760 --> 00:23:03,240
It was just a joke, come on, just a joke!

348
00:23:03,240 --> 00:23:05,660
You were serious, weren't you?

349
00:23:06,160 --> 00:23:08,380
Because there was the escape
tunnel the senpai made.

350
00:23:08,380 --> 00:23:09,560
We got saved, didn't we.

351
00:23:09,560 --> 00:23:10,260
Really.

352
00:23:11,240 --> 00:23:12,840
If I just leave him to himself like this...

353
00:23:13,240 --> 00:23:21,520
You bunch are soft!

354
00:23:22,280 --> 00:23:23,850
Whoa! Major General!

355
00:23:23,900 --> 00:23:26,780
Well, this is a fire drill, or

356
00:23:37,120 --> 00:23:39,420
Help me! Chief!

357
00:23:39,470 --> 00:23:42,760
I won't do it again! Please!

358
00:23:44,120 --> 00:23:45,400
Ohara-kun...

359
00:23:46,144 --> 00:23:49,680
Let's pretend this police box
never existed in the first place.

360
00:23:51,200 --> 00:24:05,820
Aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaah!

361
00:24:05,820 --> 00:24:13,140
You broke that radio-controlled car from the finals!
Repairing it cost 100,000 yen, 100,000!
Saying sorry doesn't fix everything in this world.

362
00:24:13,140 --> 00:24:17,980
We don't need the police.
Let's make you take responsibility, as a human being.

363
00:24:18,480 --> 00:24:21,980
Next time, let's have some man-to-man
bonding in a cypress bath, okay?

364
00:24:29,800 --> 00:24:32,640
Even if you try to stop the clock,

365
00:24:34,280 --> 00:24:37,760
time keeps passing.

366
00:24:39,360 --> 00:24:42,700
Don't keep scowling,

367
00:24:44,400 --> 00:24:47,980
laugh it off and keep living.

368
00:24:50,380 --> 00:24:53,020
Even if today

369
00:24:55,440 --> 00:24:57,920
is rainy,

370
00:25:24,920 --> 00:25:30,260
the sun is calling you
from outside the door.

